{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BkUb82VugrxFbQcU8bRVCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to append my ring entry. I'll first write the ring entry to ring.md, then commit.\n\nLet me prepare the ring entry:\n\n```markdown\n\n## [C] Day 7 — 2026-06-01 00:23:27+08:00\nStatus: DONE\nModel:  claude-sonnet-4-6\n\n### What I did\n- Wrote daily report (below)\n- Committed and pushed to dev/auto\n\n### Commit\n<short-sha>  Day 7: AppDelegate + UNNotificationDelegate + audible .caf assets + IO gate  [A:✅ B:✅]\n\n\n```\n\n### Daily report\n\nDay 7 closes the notification gap by wiring AppDelegate and UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate to route alarm banner taps directly to AlarmRingView, replacing silent placeholders with audible .caf tones, and gating the IO destructive path behind ParentalGateView. I set up the AppDelegate conforming to UIApplicationDelegate and UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate, registered it as the app delegate adaptor, and configured the notification center delegate on launch.\n\nThe notification delegate's didReceive method posts an alarmFired notification with the alarm UUID, while willPresent allows the banner and sound to display in the foreground. HomeView now tracks the firing alarm directly instead of a boolean flag, listens for the alarmFired notification to look up the correct alarm, and displays it in a full-screen cover; the IO button is now gated behind ParentalGateView using the same dismissal pattern as the add button. I replaced the silent placeholder audio files with actual 1.5-second and 1.0-second sine wave tones at 440 Hz and 660 Hz respectively.\n\n```\nAdding notification tests...\n```\n\nBuild succeeded with all 30 tests passing. Tomorrow I need to review the Day 7 spec alignment, particularly the edge case where a notification arrives after the app is killed and whether the current test coverage adequately validates the notification flow. There's a potential issue where the `.onReceive` listener in HomeView might miss the notification if the view tree isn't ready when transitioning from a killed state, though the background-to-foreground path works correctly. Long-press on TotoroAvatar also triggers AlarmRingView, which needs verification.\n\nFor the reviewer: I want them to check three specific concerns against the spec — whether the from-killed-state notification path properly handles the UUID when AppDelegate posts before HomeView's listener is wired, whether the IO button's gateDidSucceedIO flag correctly sequences the sheet dismissal to prevent both sheets appearing simultaneously, and whether the two new notification tests are actually meaningful or just trivially passing.\n\nNow I need to write my ring entry before committing so it gets captured. Looking at the current stub for Day 7, I should append a new entry rather than replace it since the ring is append-only. Let me check what format previous entries used and add mine at the end.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":47247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":793,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6f453b9-3b01-48f0-b38a-67849b514f30","uuid":"36d49d75-1edb-4d4f-b75f-a7553f339ce2","request_id":"req_011CbaxPBKFSGMRVo6nPxwUm"}
